  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Monday)\nIssued at 1112 AM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nLittle change in the overall pattern is anticipated this week. A\nfrontal boundary in the Central Plains will push farther south\nTuesday, potentially warming temps a degree or two. This may also\nallow for evening storms to at least brush the far northern \nlocations, and the potential for isolated terrain-driven \nconvection remains as well. The upper ridge is forecast to expand \nslightly to the northwest later in the week, which should reduce \nthe threat of thunderstorms even further. Additional heat \nheadlines will likely be needed. \n\nSome degree of upper ridge breakdown is still indicated by global\nmodels next week, but ensemble spread still is high and exactly\nwhen this happens remains in question at this point.",
